NAME
       xz, unxz, xzcat - compress or uncompress .xz files

SYNOPSIS
       xz [-d] [-k] [-c] [-f] [-v] [-l] [-t] [-1...-9] [-T N] [FILE]...
       unxz [FILE]...
       xzcat [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       xz compresses each FILE and replaces it with FILE.xz, keeping the
       owner, permissions and times. It usually makes smaller files than gzip
       and bzip2, but takes longer. unxz (or xz -d) turns FILE.xz back into
       FILE; xzcat prints the uncompressed contents without changing the
       file. With no FILE they work from standard input to standard output.

       tar -J (or tar -a with a .tar.xz name) uses xz for a whole archive.

OPTIONS
       -d, --decompress
              Uncompress.

       -k, --keep
              Keep the original file.

       -c, --stdout
              Write to standard output and keep the files.

       -f, --force
              Overwrite existing files.

       -l, --list
              Show the compressed and uncompressed sizes of .xz files.

       -t, --test
              Check that the files are complete and undamaged.

       -1 ... -9
              Faster (-1) or smaller (-9) compression; -6 is the default.

       -T, --threads=N
              Use N threads (0: one per CPU).

       -v, --verbose
              Show progress and the compression ratio.

       -q, --quiet
              Print no warnings.

EXAMPLES
           xz /root/big.log
           xz -l /root/big.log.xz
           xzcat /root/big.log.xz | grep error
           unxz /root/big.log.xz

SEE ALSO
       gzip(1), bzip2(1), tar(1)
